1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:01,104
Assalam o Alaikum,

2
00:00:01,184 --> 00:00:08,300
welcome to Ask Junaid where I ask you to send me whatever questions you might have that you want me to answer based on my experiences.

3
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:13,660
So a lot of people send me questions and today I'm going to read out only a few to fit in the video.

4
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:20,060
So the first one came out from Farhan Arshad. He says, Hi, I'm Farhan. I'm living in Saudi Arabia working in telecom field.

5
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:22,807
I'm getting enough salary as compared to Pakistan,

6
00:00:22,887 --> 00:00:27,580
but I'm far from family and I only get to see them annually, which makes me very sad.

7
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:28,975
Three options now.

8
00:00:29,055 --> 00:00:32,213
A, continue to live in Saudi and continue my current path.

9
00:00:32,293 --> 00:00:36,034
B, migrate to another country for better things, that is nationality.

10
00:00:36,114 --> 00:00:38,820
Or C, go back and start business in my own country.

11
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:45,184
I truly understand your sentiment where you're coming from because I also live away from my family and I know how it feels.

12
00:00:45,264 --> 00:00:48,659
But when you say you have another option to migrate to another country,

13
00:00:48,739 --> 00:00:50,373
so it's going to be the same thing.

14
00:00:50,453 --> 00:00:55,890
You're going to be away from your family for much longer because when it comes to naturalization and nationality.

15
00:00:55,970 --> 00:00:59,711
you tend to visit your home country less often and less frequent.

16
00:00:59,791 --> 00:01:01,115
If you can handle that,

17
00:01:01,195 --> 00:01:06,881
go for it because in Saudi you can spend your entire life but you won't have any sort of status.

18
00:01:06,961 --> 00:01:10,012
In that case I would suggest you move somewhere else.

19
00:01:10,092 --> 00:01:13,798
Or you said you could go back to Pakistan and start a business.

20
00:01:13,878 --> 00:01:18,307
Well, as Jim Rohn said, jobs make you wages, business make you profit.

21
00:01:18,387 --> 00:01:21,000
So I would always suggest you do a business.

22
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:28,020
business because it's always a better option rather than working for someone else. It's better to work for your own self.

23
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:33,420
If you have a very good plan, if you have enough funds, I would suggest despite the fact how

24
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:37,960
things are crazy in Pakistan, I think it still is the best place to do business.

25
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:42,900
So if you have a solid plan, if you have solid backing and funding and you think you can

26
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:47,460
live without profits for a year or two because you're not going to make profits right away, then.

27
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:53,840
I would suggest you go back home and start your own business. That's what I would do if I had a solid plan.

28
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:59,720
The next question comes from Adil Bhawani. He says, Hi Junaid, hope you're doing fantastic. I hope you are as well, Adil.

29
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:00,919
A little bit about myself.

30
00:02:00,999 --> 00:02:03,807
I have a bachelor's degree in Computer Science from Fas University.

31
00:02:03,887 --> 00:02:05,761
After that I flew to Malaysia to do my master.

32
00:02:05,841 --> 00:02:07,388
Alhamdulillah I'm done with my degree.

33
00:02:07,468 --> 00:02:08,120
Congratulations.

34
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:14,347
Now what I'm looking for is a career in business analysis or some sort of a relevant field,

35
00:02:14,427 --> 00:02:15,420
ideally in Dubai.

36
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:20,020
I have a premium account on bait.com and I have been applying for jobs on LinkedIn as well.

37
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:26,020
I would be happy if you could help me finding a job. I have also attached my resume for your reference. Very smart.

38
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:30,514
Adil, if you have seen my video about how to find jobs in Dubai,

39
00:02:30,594 --> 00:02:36,420
in that we clearly mentioned that LinkedIn is a good source of finding jobs.

40
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:41,880
But what most recruiters tend to do is they prefer having people here in Dubai.

41
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:45,620
so that they get to meet them and interview them and take things forward.

42
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:51,280
So I would suggest if you're really looking for a career in Dubai, might as well just fly down here and try your luck.

43
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:54,667
As for Bait.com, I have a friend who works for Bait.com.

44
00:02:54,747 --> 00:02:58,510
I'm gonna forward your resume to her and see where things go.

45
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:08,300
But I would suggest you should have a premium account on MonsterGirls.com because a lot of my friends had premium accounts on that website and it really helped them finding good jobs.

46
00:03:08,380 --> 00:03:09,940
So do that.

47
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:12,800
So the next question comes from someone. I'm not going to take his name for reasons.

48
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:17,260
He says, Hi. So the story goes, there was this girl I used to see.

49
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:19,700
We were both highly attached and attracted towards each other.

50
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:22,060
She was coming from a Syed and a Shia family.

51
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:25,340
So her family doesn't marry their children outside the Syed families.

52
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:29,060
Also, my family is very strict about the sectarian thing.

53
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:32,900
So I didn't get approved from my family as well.

54
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:35,660
Also, she was three years older than me and had already completed her MPhil.

55
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:40,660
while I was still an undergraduate which made my case even much weaker.

56
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:47,660
Anyway, she got married to this guy who was living abroad in the West and due to the visa reasons she had to stay behind.

57
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:51,740
During that time we used to meet each other quite often.

58
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:58,599
Somehow would try to contact her husband, but he was always very rude.

59
00:03:58,679 --> 00:04:01,754
He would ignore her messages or be very verbally abusive.

60
00:04:01,834 --> 00:04:02,280
Anyway now

61
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:06,360
She has left three days ago, and she still wants to stay in touch, but it's hard for me

62
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:11,740
I spend my nights crying since she's left. I can't stand the fact of her being in the same room with another guy

63
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:15,880
I think the sensible option would be to kill the contact between us, but I don't have to cut

64
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:20,400
I don't have the guts to end it and I don't really want to I don't want to lose her as a close friend too

65
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,480
But the transition is pretty fucking hard

66
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:25,360
What should I do? I'd appreciate if you could give me a good advice.

67
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:25,890
Well,

68
00:04:25,970 --> 00:04:38,500
I totally understand your sentiments and where you're coming from because I had a lot of friends who were a victim of sectarianism because just because two people do their namaz differently they can't be together which is really sad.

69
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:41,028
But to each their own, I don't judge it.

70
00:04:41,108 --> 00:04:47,359
I would strongly suggest you cut ties with her because what do you mean by you want to be friends with her?

71
00:04:47,439 --> 00:04:48,560
How can you come back?

72
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:53,910
come back down to be friends when you're so much emotionally involved with someone.

73
00:04:53,990 --> 00:04:55,910
You can't. It's just impossible.

74
00:04:55,990 --> 00:05:00,510
Also, with this you're influencing the idea of cheating, which is not nice.

75
00:05:00,590 --> 00:05:03,390
It could eventually come back to you because karma.

76
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:05,390
So don't do that.

77
00:05:05,470 --> 00:05:08,809
And what's gonna happen is because should you choose to stay in touch,

78
00:05:08,889 --> 00:05:14,900
one day you're gonna send her a text and she won't hear the phone because the kid was crying or she was in the kitchen.

79
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:22,900
and her husband's gonna look at the phone and he's gonna read the entire conversation and it could eventually turn ugly.

80
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:24,718
So if you really love that person,

81
00:05:24,798 --> 00:05:30,900
you don't want to put her into that situation where she could be emotionally and physically abused and hurt.

82
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:37,900
So don't do that. I would strongly suggest, see Allah ne me aankhe aage is leh nahi so that we could look forward in life and not look back.

83
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:42,860
So take lessons from your previous relationship. Cherish the good memories.

84
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:49,960
But close the chapter and move on do remember her in your prayers because that's the best thing you can do for someone you once loved

85
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:56,960
I hope you all the best in life, and I hope you would find someone better because I'm not saying better than her

86
00:05:57,040 --> 00:06:04,000
I'm saying different because God always have different and better plans for us trust me on this so thanks for sending in your questions

87
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:09,300
Yeah, if you have any questions that you want me to answer, please send in your questions in the chat

88
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:14,000
in the email below. Thank you so much for watching the video and I hope to talk to you guys soon.

89
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,260
Good bye.

